WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.293 --> 00:00:13.856
The visit with the Chesters was even shorter than the one with the Tudors.

2
00:00:15.096 --> 00:00:20.958
Jo and the boys erupted in laughing fits several more times before Amy made her excuses to leave.

3
00:00:20.978 --> 00:00:23.118
"Are you leaving already?

4
00:00:23.639 --> 00:00:28.480
The boys seem to be having so much fun with your sister," Mary remarked slyly.

5
00:00:29.616 --> 00:00:35.360
"Jo has a natural way with children," replied Amy in a composed voice, but feeling ashamed.

6
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:41.483
"We would love to stay, but I'm afraid our next appointment will require a little more traveling time."

7
00:00:41.503 --> 00:00:48.067
"Of course, I forgot that you don't have a carriage," Mary said innocently, but with a stab in

8
00:00:48.108 --> 00:00:48.708
her sentence.

9
00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:51.830
Smiling sweetly, Amy thanked Mrs.

10
00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:56.820
Chester and Mary for their hospitality then called out to Jo.

11
00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:03.386
As soon as the door of the Chester home had closed, Amy's frozen smile melted, and she turned

12
00:01:03.426 --> 00:01:04.466
to Jo in anger.

13
00:01:04.486 --> 00:01:07.989
"Can't you behave like a lady just for once?

14
00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:12.733
Why do you choose to make a fool of yourself, of me, of our family?"

15
00:01:13.053 --> 00:01:15.035
she practically yelled in the middle of the street.

16
00:01:15.055 --> 00:01:20.019
"Lower your voice, dear, people are watching," Jo said mockingly.

17
00:01:20.039 --> 00:01:21.880
"Jo! I'm serious!

18
00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:24.523
Why are you determined to ruin my life?"

19
00:01:24.903 --> 00:01:26.064
Amy cried passionately.

20
00:01:27.292 --> 00:01:29.453
"Why should I pretend to be something I'm not?"

21
00:01:29.753 --> 00:01:32.033
retorted Jo, who was close to shouting too.

22
00:01:32.053 --> 00:01:36.294
"I really don't like these people nor am I interested in their lives!"

23
00:01:37.315 --> 00:01:43.937
Regaining her composure, Amy breathed deeply and said, "Because that's how people will learn to respect us and

24
00:01:44.077 --> 00:01:44.877
treat us better."

25
00:01:45.977 --> 00:01:49.338
Shaking her head, Jo said, "You're wrong, Amy.

26
00:01:49.858 --> 00:01:53.619
No matter how nice we are to them, they won't think of us as their equal.

27
00:01:54.339 --> 00:01:56.320
I thought you realized that after your party."

28
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.521
The two sisters walked in silence for a while, then Amy spoke up.

29
00:02:00.541 --> 00:02:06.223
"Maybe you're right, but I still believe that good will come if we try to show kindness to

30
00:02:06.323 --> 00:02:08.363
others regardless of how they see us."

31
00:02:08.383 --> 00:02:14.305
"That's why you are a dreamer, Amy," acknowledged Jo, "and I love you for it.

32
00:02:15.285 --> 00:02:15.785
But me?

33
00:02:16.405 --> 00:02:21.387
I'm practical and realistic and I don't believe that I have to change just to make another person

34
00:02:21.427 --> 00:02:25.128
happy." "Then I won't ask you to," Amy said.

35
00:02:25.916 --> 00:02:28.498
"You are you, Jo, and I love you for it too."

36
00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:33.781
Stopping in front of Aunt March's house, the two sisters gave each other a quick hug.

37
00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:35.723
"Can I be me now?"

38
00:02:36.123 --> 00:02:37.044
Jo asked playfully.

39
00:02:37.064 --> 00:02:39.425
"Of course," smiled Amy.

40
00:02:39.445 --> 00:02:43.008
"Besides, Aunt March knows your true colors anyway."

41
00:02:44.929 --> 00:02:50.092
Giggling, the sisters held hands as they walked up toward the large mansion.

42
00:02:51.473 --> 00:02:55.076
Aunt March's housemaid Esther brought the girls to the west wing sitting room.

43
00:02:56.412 --> 00:03:02.514
(Aunt March's mansion was so gigantic that she had three sitting rooms, one in each direction except for

44
00:03:02.594 --> 00:03:09.636
east.) The old lady sat in her "throne," as Jo called her large velvet armchair with gold armrests

45
00:03:09.776 --> 00:03:10.856
and satin cushions.

46
00:03:12.437 --> 00:03:18.278
Aunt March was feeding crackers to Polly who, upon seeing them, screeched loudly, "Mind your mouth!"

47
00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:24.620
"Hello, Aunt March," said Amy, walking over and kissing her on both cheeks.

48
00:03:25.796 --> 00:03:30.257
Jo stood awkwardly because in all the years she had come to work at this house, she had

49
00:03:30.317 --> 00:03:31.938
never greeted her aunt with a kiss.

50
00:03:31.958 --> 00:03:35.919
"What are you standing there for like a stone statue?"

51
00:03:36.239 --> 00:03:37.739
the old lady snapped at Jo.

52
00:03:37.759 --> 00:03:39.740
"Polly needs more crackers."

53
00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.901
"Crackers!" screeched the parrot.

54
00:03:43.661 --> 00:03:48.442
Without another word, Jo turned around and headed toward the kitchen to do as Aunt March told her.

55
00:03:49.422 --> 00:03:53.924
When she returned with the crackers and a dish of clean water for the bird, Jo saw a

56
00:03:54.164 --> 00:04:00.163
rare sight: the deep lines on her aunt's face had softened and the corners of her mouth lifted

57
00:04:00.223 --> 00:04:01.103
upward in a smile.

58
00:04:01.123 --> 00:04:06.726
"Now Aunt March, I insist that you let me adjust these pillows back here.

59
00:04:07.407 --> 00:04:13.310
You don't look very comfortable sitting there," said Amy, carefully rearranging the cushions on Aunt March's chair.

60
00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:19.594
"I'm fine," Aunt March said in a much more tender voice than she had ever used with Jo.

61
00:04:20.735 --> 00:04:22.916
"Where is that sister of yours?

62
00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.641
Has she gone to make her own crackers?

63
00:04:26.002 --> 00:04:27.482
Polly is starving here."

64
00:04:27.502 --> 00:04:33.786
"Here we go," said Jo in an overly cheery voice, as she pushed the crackers into Polly's face.

65
00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:40.009
"Let me do it, Jo," Amy said, taking the dish from her and expertly breaking off pieces to

66
00:04:40.069 --> 00:04:40.750
feed the bird.

67
00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.732
Jo had to admit that Amy excelled at her job.

68
00:04:46.113 --> 00:04:50.895
Even though Jo knew Amy was not fond of the bird, at that moment, you could not see

69
00:04:50.995 --> 00:04:55.623
Amy's true feelings, because she treated Polly as gently as Aunt March did.

70
00:04:56.644 --> 00:05:02.369
When Esther brought in the tea and biscuits, Jo wandered over to the bookshelves to see if Aunt

71
00:05:02.409 --> 00:05:06.112
March had gotten any new books since she stopped working for her.

72
00:05:06.132 --> 00:05:11.597
"Josephine, I'd like to hear a story," Aunt March called to her.

73
00:05:11.617 --> 00:05:16.722
"Amy here is a darling, but no one can read a story like you can, dear."

74
00:05:17.763 --> 00:05:22.853
Feeling touched, Jo selected a new book that she thought would be interesting and took it over to

75
00:05:22.933 --> 00:05:23.373
Aunt March.

76
00:05:24.634 --> 00:05:26.734
"No. That one's terribly boring.

77
00:05:27.274 --> 00:05:29.975
Bring Stories from the Garden," said her aunt.

78
00:05:29.995 --> 00:05:34.836
"But doesn't The Pirate's Treasure Box sound more exciting and adventurous?"

79
00:05:35.236 --> 00:05:39.277
Jo asked persuasively, since the title was especially appealing to her.

80
00:05:39.297 --> 00:05:42.358
"I don't care for that one, Josephine.

81
00:05:42.858 --> 00:05:45.379
The other one is better," Aunt March said firmly.

82
00:05:45.399 --> 00:05:51.795
"Yes, Aunt March," Jo said, bringing the garden stories book and sitting down next to her aunt.

83
00:05:52.916 --> 00:05:57.400
Amy poured the tea and chose some biscuits for Aunt March while Jo opened the book to read.

84
00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:04.667
"Girls, there is something I want to discuss with you," Aunt March began as she accepted the teacup

85
00:06:04.687 --> 00:06:09.492
from Amy with one hand, while placing the other on Jo's arm to stop her from reading.

86
00:06:10.252 --> 00:06:13.896
The sisters looked at her expectantly, waiting for her to continue.

87
00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:19.624
"As you know, every summer I travel to Europe for a holiday," said Aunt March.

88
00:06:19.644 --> 00:06:26.630
"This year I have chosen to spend the entire year abroad as my health has worsened and the

89
00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:29.352
warmer climates seem to improve it somewhat."

90
00:06:29.372 --> 00:06:34.496
"Of course, Aunt March, your health is the main priority," said Amy.

91
00:06:35.397 --> 00:06:37.198
Nodding at her, Aunt March continued.

92
00:06:37.598 --> 00:06:45.148
"However, the doctor recommends that I travel with a companion Aunt March chose to pause here, sip her

93
00:06:45.169 --> 00:06:47.571
tea, and adjust a cushion before continuing.

94
00:06:48.431 --> 00:06:53.456
Meanwhile, both Jo and Amy, realizing what Aunt March was about to announce, held their breath.

95
00:06:54.356 --> 00:06:58.940
Each girl hoped her heart wouldn't jump out of her chest because it was beating so fast.

96
00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:04.746
"I must confess it was a hard decision for me to make," said Aunt March.

97
00:07:04.766 --> 00:07:11.752
"Whether you believe it or not, I am fond of both of you for obviously different reasons.

98
00:07:12.476 --> 00:07:19.201
However, as I will be covering all expenses for this trip, I expect my companion to be someone

99
00:07:19.241 --> 00:07:21.482
who will do exactly as I say."

100
00:07:22.743 --> 00:07:28.167
Jo could hardly sit still since her dream of traveling to Europe seemed about to come true in

101
00:07:28.207 --> 00:07:29.208
the next few seconds.

102
00:07:30.188 --> 00:07:36.272
Then looking at each girl long and hard, Aunt March held out her hand and said, "Therefore, I've

103
00:07:36.292 --> 00:07:39.054
decided to take Amy to Europe with me."
